A||||3||Cheever2||How do I backup emails & address book?||||2||
Z||000000||Cheever2||03-13-2001||09:24 AM||||Previously I have been backing up my family's files whenever I think of it, which hasn't been often enough.  So I want to start a standard routine of weekly backups onto rewriteable CD's.  <P>Besides our individual folders, is there also a way to make backups of our Outlook Express emails and the address book?  Where are those things stored?<P>I have a Compaq Presario.<BR><P>------------------<BR><I>Chuck Hodges</I>||||reg||2
Z||000001||lou_dias||03-13-2001||12:31 PM||||Just EXPORT them in the FILE menu to a text (CSV) file.<BR>If you lose your email, you can always IMPORT them later.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cheever2||03-13-2001||03:26 PM||||The address book exported, but trying to export the messages gave an error: "The export could not be performed. An error occurred while initializing MAPI".<BR>||||reg||6
Z||000003||Cheever2||03-14-2001||01:07 PM||||I had to hilite the folder (inbox was all I wanted to backup), then click File, then, Folder, then Compact.  This puts them into C:\Windows\Application Data\Identities.  I copied this to a folder in C:\ and using Adaptec CD Creator, backed it up along with the other folders I needed to save.<BR> <BR>Some other day I will do a test run of restoring it all, to ensure I can actually use what I have backed up, if it is ever needed.<P>I'm on my third PC since last June, so I'm very nervous about losing everything again.  And my wife has started using the puter for her teaching stuff.  That would be a big loss, even though I try to get her saving to diskette as well as hard drive.<P>Next, I want to find out how to save my Favorites, including websites.  I'm sure it's easy, just haven't looked yet.<BR>||||reg||6
